other_item_heading_inside_body)"},{"step":"ending_or_current_basis","what":"provisional NO, but no job found a whole-order-end candidate"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:10094\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1949-12-28/pdf/FR-1949-12-28.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 87d79810581ca1d1760484fabe92649987a0b0dd75182577c54f20314743bf5b\nLocation: 14 FR 7726, PDF pages 4-4 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 4 of 28 ===\n7726 THE PRESIDENT\nPA R T I\nTo the end that the said trade agree­\nment specified in the seventh recital of \nthis proclamation may be carried out:\n(a) Subject to the provisions of sub­\ndivision (b) of this part, such modifica­\ntions of existing duties and other import \nrestrictions of the United States of \nAmerica and such continuance of exist­\ning customs or excise treatment of arti­\ncles imported into the United States of \nAmerica as are specified or provided for \nin paragraphs 1  to 13 of the said proto­\ncol of accession and in part I of, and the \ngeneral notes in, schedule XX in annex \nA thereto shall be effective on and after \nJanuary 1, 1950.\n(b) The application of the provisions \nof subdivision (a) of this part shall be \nsubject to the applicable terms, condi­\ntions, and qualifications set forth in \nparagraphs 1  to 13 of the said protocol of \naccession, in part I of, and the general \nnotes in, schedule XX in annex A thereto, \nin parts I, II, and III of the said general \nagreement, ","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10094.txt","sha256":"b490f16857a2caaa096e9d8ec12678d6e8cf7791972ad21ada99ba205440d5ac","source":{"line":564,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"ef9a6b2ac915a4a43750e9bb